From: SamuriHL <samurihl@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 10:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] HDMV VM: fix the BC (bit compare) instruction to spec semantics

The BC compare executed the next instruction iff (dst & ~src) == 0 - a
subset test that never checks whether the requested bits are SET, only
that no bits outside the mask are. The BD-ROM spec defines BC as a plain
bitwise AND: the condition passes when any tested bit is set.

Real authoring confirms it: the S&M UHD Benchmark's MovieObject enumerates
the UHD capability PSR bits one at a time (BC PSR25,0x01 / 0x02 / 0x04 /
0x20 -> one GPR flag per format, then sums player+display flags per
format). That per-bit enumeration is only meaningful under "is this bit
set" - under the subset test a multi-bit capability register fails every
single-bit test, which forced players to mis-report a single exclusive
format bit to branch correctly. Capability PSRs (25/26) are genuine OR
sets, like PSR15; with BC fixed they can carry the truth.

Analysis credit: Hendrik Leppkes spotted the inverted implementation.
---
 src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c b/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c
--- a/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c
+++ b/src/libbluray/hdmv/hdmv_vm.c
@@ -1134,7 +1134,11 @@ static int _hdmv_step(HDMV_VM *p)
                 BD_DEBUG(DBG_HDMV|DBG_CRIT, "missing operand in BRANCH/JUMP opcode 0x%08x\n", *(uint32_t*)insn);
             }
             switch (insn->cmp_opt) {
-                case INSN_BC: p->pc += !!(dst & ~src); break;
+                /* spec: plain bitwise AND - condition passes when any tested
+                 * bit is set. The previous (dst & ~src) subset test never
+                 * checked the requested bits at all and broke capability-set
+                 * registers (PSR25/26) for every disc enumerating them. */
+                case INSN_BC: p->pc += !(dst & src); break;
                 case INSN_EQ: p->pc += !(dst == src); break;
                 case INSN_NE: p->pc += !(dst != src); break;
                 case INSN_GE: p->pc += !(dst >= src); break;
